          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif'>Ethical Considerations &amp; Algorithmic Safeguards</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif'>Fairness &amp; Bias:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif'> Demographic variables (e.g., Gender, Income Category) are displayed strictly to audit potential systemic bias and ensure retention strategies do not create a disparate impact across vulnerable groups.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif'>Data Privacy &amp; Gaps:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif'> Categories marked as </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif' italic='true'>Unknown</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif'> (representing ~11% of income data and ~15% of education data) reflect explicit customer non-disclosure. Models should avoid inferring missing socioeconomic attributes without explicit consent. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif'>Non-Causal Insights:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Google Sans Text,sans-serif'> Risk scores and visual trends represent statistical correlation rather than direct causation. Automated interventions should include human oversight.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
